/-!
# Log derivations and the log Jacobian ideal

This file proves parts of Volume V, Section 4.4 of the handbook. It defines the derivations that
are tangent to a set and the ideal of their values. In the polynomial model `B = k[x_i : i ∈ σ]`
with the divisor `x_i = 0` for `i ∈ Δ`, it shows that this ideal is the log Jacobian ideal
`Singularity.logJacobian Δ` of the repository. It also proves the transformation law of
Lemma 4.4.18, part 1, in this model.

## Main definitions

* `stableDerivations k I`: the derivations of `B` over `k` that map the ideal `I` into `I`.
* `tangentDerivations k G`: the module `T_G(B)` of the derivations tangent to `G`
  (Definition 4.4.2).
* `derivationIdeal k M f`: the ideal of the values `δ(f)` for `δ ∈ M`. For `M = T_G(B)` this is
  `J_G(f)` (Definition 4.4.2).
* `logDerivations Δ`, `logDerivation Δ`: the derivations `x_i ∂_i` for `i ∈ Δ` and `∂_j` for
  `j ∉ Δ`.

## Main results

* `lie_mem_tangentDerivations`: `T_G` is closed under the bracket (Lemma 4.4.3, part 2, for
  the bracket).
* `derivationIdeal_add_pow`: `J(f + h^p) = J(f)` in characteristic `p` (Lemma 4.4.4, part 1).
  The polynomial form is `Singularity.logJacobian_add_pow` of the repository.
* `tangentDerivations_mono`, `derivationIdeal_mono`: a larger `G` gives a smaller `T_G` and a
  smaller `J_G(f)` (Lemma 4.4.4, part 3).
* `derivation_sum_pow_mul_pow`: if `f = ∑_{i < p} c_i^p t^i`, then `δ(f) = c δ(t)` with
  `c = ∑ i c_i^p t^(i-1)`, for each derivation `δ` (Lemma 4.4.5, the step from part 2 to
  part 3, written with derivations).
* `derivation_eq_sum_pderiv`, `lie_pderiv_pderiv`: each derivation of `k[x]` is
  `∑ δ(x_i) ∂_i`, and the `∂_i` commute (Lemma 4.4.1, parts 2 and 3, polynomial model).
* `mem_tangentDerivations_X_iff`, `tangentDerivations_X_eq_span`,
  `linearIndependent_logDerivation`: `T_Δ` is the free module with the basis `x_i ∂_i`
  (`i ∈ Δ`), `∂_j` (`j ∉ Δ`) (Lemma 4.4.3, part 1, polynomial model).
* `derivationIdeal_tangentDerivations_X`: `J_Δ(f) = logJacobian Δ f` (Lemma 4.4.3, part 4,
  polynomial model).
* `logJacobian_le_of_subset`: `Δ ⊆ Δ'` gives `J_Δ'(f) ⊆ J_Δ(f)` (Lemma 4.4.4, part 3).
* `logJacobian_eq_bot_iff_pderiv`, `exists_eq_pow_iff_pderiv_eq_zero`, `logJacobian_eq_bot_iff`:
  over a perfect field of characteristic `p`, `J_Δ(f) = 0` if and only if `f` is a `p`-th power
  in `k[x]` (Lemma 4.4.4, part 2, polynomial model).
* `logJacobian_eq_span_of_monomial`: for `t = x^a` with `p ∣ a_i` for `i ∉ Δ` and `p ∤ a_i` for
  some `i ∈ Δ`, and `f = ∑_{i < p} c_i^p t^i` with polynomials `c_i`, the ideal `J_Δ(f)` is the
  principal ideal `(c t)` (Proposition 4.4.15, part 1, polynomial model with the unit `u = 1`).
* `span_eq_top_of_span_eq_span_singleton`: if an ideal `(S)` of a domain is `(m)` with `m ≠ 0`,
  then the cofactors `s / m` generate the unit ideal (the first step of the proof of
  Theorem 4.4.16).
* `tangentDerivations_inf_stable_eq_span`, `derivationIdeal_center`: the derivations tangent to
  the divisor and to the center `(x_i : i ∈ S)` are generated by `x_i ∂_i` (`i ∈ Δ`), `∂_l`
  (`l ∉ Δ`, `l ∉ S`) and `x_m ∂_l` (`l ∉ Δ`, `l ∈ S`, `m ∈ S`), and their values give the
  ideal `logJacobianCenter Δ S` (Lemma 4.4.18, part 1, polynomial model).
* `logJacobianCenter_of_subset`: for a stratum, `S ⊆ Δ`, the ideal of the center is
  `J_Δ(f)` (Corollary 4.4.19, part 2, first claim, polynomial model).

## What is not proved

* Lemma 4.4.1 for a regular local ring essentially of finite type over `k`: the freeness of
  `Ω_{R/k}`, the extension of derivations to the fraction field, and `∂^p = 0`. Only the
  polynomial model is done, and `∂^p = 0` is not done there.
* Lemma 4.4.3, part 2, for `δ ↦ δ^p`: this needs the Leibniz rule for `δ^p` in characteristic
  `p`, which is not proved here. Part 3 (the module `Ω_R(log D)`) is not done.
* Lemma 4.4.4, part 2, for the fraction field `E`: the polynomial model proves `f = g^p` in
  `k[x]`, not `f ∈ E^p` for a regular local ring.
* Lemma 4.4.5: the equivalence of parts 1 and 2 and the step from part 3 to part 2 need
  `p`-bases and Kähler differentials of `E`. Only the step from part 2 to part 3 is done.
* Proposition 4.4.15: the unit `u`, the residual type (part 2), and the general regular local
  ring are not done.
* Theorem 4.4.16 and Corollary 4.4.17: only the first step of the proof is done. The Euler type
  derivations, the gradings and the construction of the first integral are not formalized.
* Lemma 4.4.18, part 2, and Corollary 4.4.19, part 1: the localizations of the charts are not
  formalized here. The chart law of the polynomial model is in
  `Singularity.Invariant.LogJacobianCenter` (`map_centerChart_logJacobianCenter_le`,
  `span_mul_logJacobian_centerChart_le`), and `logJacobianCenter_le` gives
  `J_{D,Z}(f) ⊆ J_D(f)`.
-/

open MvPolynomial

namespace Singularity

/-! ### Derivations tangent to a set -/

section General

variable (k : Type*) {B : Type*} [CommRing k] [CommRing B] [Algebra k B]

/-- The derivations of `B` over `k` that map the ideal `I` into `I`. -/
def stableDerivations (I : Ideal B) : Submodule B (Derivation k B B) where
  carrier := {δ | ∀ b ∈ I, δ b ∈ I}
  add_mem' {δ δ'} hδ hδ' b hb := by
    rw [Derivation.add_apply]
    exact I.add_mem (hδ b hb) (hδ' b hb)
  zero_mem' b _ := by
    rw [Derivation.zero_apply]
    exact I.zero_mem
  smul_mem' c δ hδ b hb := by
    rw [Derivation.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul]
    exact I.mul_mem_left c (hδ b hb)

/-- The module `T_G(B)` of the derivations tangent to `G`: the derivations that map `gB` into
`gB` for each `g ∈ G` (Volume V, Definition 4.4.2 of the handbook). -/
def tangentDerivations (G : Set B) : Submodule B (Derivation k B B) :=
  ⨅ g ∈ G, stableDerivations k (Ideal.span {g})

/-- The evaluation `δ ↦ δ(f)`, a `B`-linear map. -/
def evalDerivation (f : B) : Derivation k B B →ₗ[B] B where
  toFun δ := δ f
  map_add' _ _ := by simp
  map_smul' _ _ := by simp

/-- The ideal of the values `δ(f)` for `δ ∈ M`. For `M = T_G(B)` it is the ideal `J_G(f)` of
Volume V, Definition 4.4.2 of the handbook. -/
def derivationIdeal (M : Submodule B (Derivation k B B)) (f : B) : Ideal B :=
  M.map (evalDerivation k f)

variable {k}

theorem evalDerivation_apply (f : B) (δ : Derivation k B B) : evalDerivation k f δ = δ f := rfl

theorem mem_stableDerivations {I : Ideal B} {δ : Derivation k B B} :
    δ ∈ stableDerivations k I ↔ ∀ b ∈ I, δ b ∈ I := Iff.rfl

theorem mem_tangentDerivations {G : Set B} {δ : Derivation k B B} :
    δ ∈ tangentDerivations k G ↔ ∀ g ∈ G, ∀ b ∈ Ideal.span {g}, δ b ∈ Ideal.span {g} := by
  simp only [tangentDerivations, Submodule.mem_iInf, mem_stableDerivations]

theorem mem_derivationIdeal {M : Submodule B (Derivation k B B)} {f x : B} :
    x ∈ derivationIdeal k M f ↔ ∃ δ ∈ M, δ f = x := Submodule.mem_map

/-- The bracket of two derivations that map `I` into `I` maps `I` into `I`. -/
theorem lie_mem_stableDerivations {I : Ideal B} {δ δ' : Derivation k B B}
    (hδ : δ ∈ stableDerivations k I) (hδ' : δ' ∈ stableDerivations k I) :
    ⁅δ, δ'⁆ ∈ stableDerivations k I := fun b hb => by
  rw [Derivation.commutator_apply]
  exact I.sub_mem (hδ _ (hδ' b hb)) (hδ' _ (hδ b hb))

/-- `T_G` is closed under the bracket (Volume V, Lemma 4.4.3, part 2, for the bracket). -/
theorem lie_mem_tangentDerivations {G : Set B} {δ δ' : Derivation k B B}
    (hδ : δ ∈ tangentDerivations k G) (hδ' : δ' ∈ tangentDerivations k G) :
    ⁅δ, δ'⁆ ∈ tangentDerivations k G := by
  simp only [tangentDerivations, Submodule.mem_iInf] at hδ hδ' ⊢
  exact fun g hg => lie_mem_stableDerivations (hδ g hg) (hδ' g hg)

/-- A larger set gives fewer tangent derivations (Volume V, Lemma 4.4.4, part 3). -/
theorem tangentDerivations_mono {G G' : Set B} (h : G ⊆ G') :
    tangentDerivations k G' ≤ tangentDerivations k G := fun _ hδ =>
  mem_tangentDerivations.2 fun g hg => mem_tangentDerivations.1 hδ g (h hg)

theorem derivationIdeal_mono {M M' : Submodule B (Derivation k B B)} (h : M ≤ M') (f : B) :
    derivationIdeal k M f ≤ derivationIdeal k M' f :=
  Submodule.map_mono h

/-- In characteristic `p` each derivation kills the `p`-th powers. -/
theorem derivation_pow_char {p : ℕ} [CharP B p] (δ : Derivation k B B) (h : B) :
    δ (h ^ p) = 0 := by
  rw [Derivation.leibniz_pow, nsmul_eq_mul, CharP.cast_eq_zero, zero_mul]

/-- `J(f + h^p) = J(f)` in characteristic `p` (Volume V, Lemma 4.4.4, part 1). -/
theorem derivationIdeal_add_pow {p : ℕ} [CharP B p] (M : Submodule B (Derivation k B B))
    (f h : B) : derivationIdeal k M (f + h ^ p) = derivationIdeal k M f := by
  ext x
  simp only [mem_derivationIdeal, map_add, derivation_pow_char, add_zero]

/-- If `f = ∑_{i < p} c_i^p t^i`, then `δ(f) = c δ(t)` with `c = ∑_{i < p} i c_i^p t^(i-1)`, for
each derivation `δ` (Volume V, Lemma 4.4.5, the step from part 2 to part 3, for derivations). -/
theorem derivation_sum_pow_mul_pow {p : ℕ} [CharP B p] (δ : Derivation k B B) (c : Fin p → B)
    (t : B) : δ (∑ i : Fin p, c i ^ p * t ^ (i : ℕ)) =
      (∑ i : Fin p, ((i : ℕ) : B) * c i ^ p * t ^ ((i : ℕ) - 1)) * δ t := by
  rw [map_sum, Finset.sum_mul]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
  rw [Derivation.leibniz, derivation_pow_char (p := p) δ (c i), smul_zero, add_zero,
    Derivation.leibniz_pow,
    smul_eq_mul, nsmul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul]
  ring

/-- If an ideal `(S)` of a domain is the principal ideal `(m)` with `m ≠ 0`, then the cofactors
`c` with `m c ∈ S` generate the unit ideal. This is the first step of the proof of Volume V,
Theorem 4.4.16 of the handbook. -/
theorem span_eq_top_of_span_eq_span_singleton [IsDomain B] {S : Set B} {m : B} (hm : m ≠ 0)
    (h : Ideal.span S = Ideal.span {m}) : Ideal.span {c | m * c ∈ S} = ⊤ := by
  have hle : Ideal.span S ≤ Ideal.span {m} * Ideal.span {c | m * c ∈ S} := by
    refine Ideal.span_le.2 fun s hs => ?_
    have hsm : s ∈ Ideal.span {m} := h ▸ Ideal.subset_span hs
    obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.1 hsm
    have hc : c ∈ {c | m * c ∈ S} := by
      show m * c ∈ S
      rw [mul_comm]
      exact hs
    have hmul := Ideal.mul_mem_mul (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self m) (Ideal.subset_span hc)
    rw [mul_comm c m]
    exact hmul
  have hmS : m ∈ Ideal.span S := h ▸ Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self m
  obtain ⟨z, hz, hmz⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton_mul.1 (hle hmS)
  have hz1 : z = 1 := mul_left_cancel₀ hm (hmz.trans (mul_one m).symm)
  exact (Ideal.eq_top_iff_one _).2 (hz1 ▸ hz)

end General

/-! ### The polynomial model -/

section Poly

variable {σ k : Type*} [CommRing k] [DecidableEq σ]

/-- The value of `c ∂_i` at the variable `x_l`. -/
theorem smul_pderiv_X (c : MvPolynomial σ k) (i l : σ) :
    (c • pderiv i) (X l) = if l = i then c else 0 := by
  rw [Derivation.smul_apply, pderiv_X, Pi.single_apply, smul_eq_mul]
  split_ifs <;> simp

/-- Each derivation of `k[x]` is `∑ δ(x_i) ∂_i` (Volume V, Lemma 4.4.1, part 2, polynomial
model). -/
theorem derivation_eq_sum_pderiv [Fintype σ]
    (δ : Derivation k (MvPolynomial σ k) (MvPolynomial σ k)) :
    δ = ∑ i, δ (X i) • pderiv i := by
  refine derivation_ext fun l => ?_
  have hs := map_sum (evalDerivation k (X l : MvPolynomial σ k))
    (fun i => δ (X i) • pderiv (R := k) i) Finset.univ
  simp only [evalDerivation_apply] at hs
  rw [hs]
  simp only [smul_pderiv_X, Finset.sum_ite_eq, Finset.mem_univ, ite_true]

/-- The partial derivatives commute (Volume V, Lemma 4.4.1, part 3, polynomial model). -/
theorem lie_pderiv_pderiv (i j : σ) :
    ⁅pderiv (R := k) (σ := σ) i, pderiv (R := k) (σ := σ) j⁆ = 0 := by
  refine derivation_ext fun l => ?_
  rw [Derivation.commutator_apply, pderiv_X, pderiv_X, Derivation.zero_apply]
  simp only [Pi.single_apply]
  split_ifs <;> simp

omit [DecidableEq σ] in
/-- A derivation is tangent to the divisor `x_i = 0`, `i ∈ Δ`, if and only if `δ(x_i) ∈ (x_i)`
for each `i ∈ Δ`. -/
theorem mem_tangentDerivations_X_iff {Δ : Set σ}
    {δ : Derivation k (MvPolynomial σ k) (MvPolynomial σ k)} :
    δ ∈ tangentDerivations k (X '' Δ) ↔ ∀ i ∈ Δ, δ (X i) ∈ Ideal.span {X i} := by
  rw [mem_tangentDerivations]
  constructor
  · intro h i hi
    exact h _ ⟨i, hi, rfl⟩ _ (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _)
  · rintro h _ ⟨i, hi, rfl⟩ b hb
    obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.1 hb
    rw [Derivation.leibniz, smul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul]
    exact Ideal.add_mem _ (Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (h i hi))
      (Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _))

/-- The log derivations `x_i ∂_i` for `i ∈ Δ` and `∂_j` for `j ∉ Δ`, as a set. -/
abbrev logDerivations (Δ : Finset σ) :
    Set (Derivation k (MvPolynomial σ k) (MvPolynomial σ k)) :=
  (fun i => X (R := k) i • pderiv i) '' (Δ : Set σ) ∪
    (fun j => pderiv (R := k) j) '' (Δ : Set σ)ᶜ

/-- The log derivations as a family: `x_i ∂_i` for `i ∈ Δ` and `∂_i` for `i ∉ Δ`. -/
noncomputable def logDerivation (Δ : Finset σ) (i : σ) :
    Derivation k (MvPolynomial σ k) (MvPolynomial σ k) :=
  if i ∈ Δ then X (R := k) i • pderiv i else pderiv i

theorem X_smul_pderiv_mem_tangentDerivations (Δ : Set σ) (i : σ) :
    X (R := k) i • pderiv (R := k) i ∈
      tangentDerivations k (X '' Δ) := by
  refine mem_tangentDerivations_X_iff.2 fun l _ => ?_
  rw [smul_pderiv_X]
  split_ifs with h
  · subst h
    exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _
  · exact zero_mem _

omit [DecidableEq σ] in
theorem pderiv_mem_tangentDerivations {Δ : Set σ} {j : σ} (hj : j ∉ Δ) :
    (pderiv j : Derivation k (MvPolynomial σ k) (MvPolynomial σ k)) ∈
      tangentDerivations k (X '' Δ) := by
  refine mem_tangentDerivations_X_iff.2 fun l hl => ?_
  have hlj : l ≠ j := fun h => hj (h ▸ hl)
  rw [pderiv_X_of_ne hlj]
  exact zero_mem _

/-- `T_Δ` is generated by `x_i ∂_i` (`i ∈ Δ`) and `∂_j` (`j ∉ Δ`) (Volume V, Lemma 4.4.3,
part 1, polynomial model). -/
theorem tangentDerivations_X_eq_span [Fintype σ] (Δ : Finset σ) :
    tangentDerivations k (X '' (Δ : Set σ)) =
      Submodule.span (MvPolynomial σ k) (logDerivations (k := k) Δ) := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun δ hδ => ?_) (Submodule.span_le.2 ?_)
  · rw [derivation_eq_sum_pderiv δ]
    refine Submodule.sum_mem _ fun i _ => ?_
    by_cases hi : i ∈ Δ
    · obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.1 (mem_tangentDerivations_X_iff.1 hδ i hi)
      rw [← hc, mul_smul]
      exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.subset_span (Or.inl ⟨i, hi, rfl⟩))
    · exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.subset_span (Or.inr ⟨i, hi, rfl⟩))
  · rintro _ (⟨i, -, rfl⟩ | ⟨j, hj, rfl⟩)
    · exact X_smul_pderiv_mem_tangentDerivations _ i
    · exact pderiv_mem_tangentDerivations hj

/-- The log derivations are linearly independent over `k[x]` (Volume V, Lemma 4.4.3, part 1,
polynomial model). With `tangentDerivations_X_eq_span` they are a basis of `T_Δ`. -/
theorem linearIndependent_logDerivation [Fintype σ] (Δ : Finset σ) :
    LinearIndependent (MvPolynomial σ k) (logDerivation (k := k) Δ) := by
  rw [Fintype.linearIndependent_iff]
  intro g hg l
  have hterm : ∀ i, (g i • logDerivation (k := k) Δ i) (X l) =
      if i = l then g l * (if l ∈ Δ then X l else 1) else 0 := by
    intro i
    rw [Derivation.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul]
    by_cases hil : i = l
    · subst hil
      by_cases hi : i ∈ Δ <;> simp [logDerivation, hi]
    · have hli : l ≠ i := fun h => hil h.symm
      by_cases hi : i ∈ Δ <;> simp [logDerivation, hi, hil, hli]
  have hs := map_sum (evalDerivation k (X l : MvPolynomial σ k))
    (fun i => g i • logDerivation (k := k) Δ i) Finset.univ
  simp only [evalDerivation_apply, hterm, Finset.sum_ite_eq', Finset.mem_univ, ite_true] at hs
  rw [hg, Derivation.zero_apply] at hs
  by_cases hl : l ∈ Δ
  · simp only [hl, ↓reduceIte] at hs
    exact isRegular_X.right (hs.symm.trans (zero_mul _).symm)
  · simp only [hl, ↓reduceIte, mul_one] at hs
    exact hs.symm

/-- The ideal of the values of `T_Δ` at `g` is the log Jacobian ideal `logJacobian Δ g`
(Volume V, Lemma 4.4.3, part 4, polynomial model). -/
theorem derivationIdeal_tangentDerivations_X [Fintype σ] (Δ : Finset σ) (g : MvPolynomial σ k) :
    derivationIdeal k (tangentDerivations k (X '' (Δ : Set σ))) g = logJacobian Δ g := by
  rw [derivationIdeal, tangentDerivations_X_eq_span, Submodule.map_span, logDerivations,
    Set.image_union, Set.image_image, Set.image_image, logJacobian]
  rfl

/-- A larger divisor gives a smaller log Jacobian ideal (Volume V, Lemma 4.4.4, part 3,
polynomial model). -/
theorem logJacobian_le_of_subset {Δ Δ' : Finset σ} (h : Δ ⊆ Δ') (g : MvPolynomial σ k) :
    logJacobian Δ' g ≤ logJacobian Δ g := by
  refine Ideal.span_le.2 ?_
  rintro _ (⟨i, -, rfl⟩ | ⟨j, hj, rfl⟩)
  · by_cases hiΔ : i ∈ Δ
    · exact Ideal.subset_span (Or.inl ⟨i, hiΔ, rfl⟩)
    · exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (Ideal.subset_span (Or.inr ⟨i, hiΔ, rfl⟩))
  · exact Ideal.subset_span (Or.inr ⟨j, fun hjΔ => hj (h hjΔ), rfl⟩)

/-- `J_Δ(f) = 0` if and only if all the partial derivatives of `f` vanish. -/
theorem logJacobian_eq_bot_iff_pderiv {Δ : Finset σ} {f : MvPolynomial σ k} :
    logJacobian Δ f = ⊥ ↔ ∀ i, pderiv i f = 0 := by
  rw [logJacobian, Ideal.span_eq_bot]
  constructor
  · intro h i
    by_cases hi : i ∈ Δ
    · have h0 : X i * pderiv i f = 0 := h _ (Or.inl ⟨i, hi, rfl⟩)
      exact isRegular_X.left (h0.trans (mul_zero _).symm)
    · exact h _ (Or.inr ⟨i, hi, rfl⟩)
  · rintro h _ (⟨i, -, rfl⟩ | ⟨j, -, rfl⟩)
    · show X i * pderiv i f = 0
      rw [h i, mul_zero]
    · exact h j

end Poly

section Perfect

variable {σ k : Type*} [Field k] {p : ℕ} [Fact p.Prime] [CharP k p]

omit [Fact p.Prime] in
/-- If all the partial derivatives of `f` vanish, then `p` divides each exponent of each monomial
of `f`. -/
theorem dvd_of_pderiv_eq_zero {f : MvPolynomial σ k} (h : ∀ i, pderiv i f = 0) {a : σ →₀ ℕ}
    (ha : a ∈ f.support) (i : σ) : p ∣ a i := by
  classical
  by_cases hai : a i = 0
  · rw [hai]
    exact dvd_zero p
  set m := a - Finsupp.single i 1 with hm
  have hma : m + Finsupp.single i 1 = a :=
    tsub_add_cancel_of_le (Finsupp.single_le_iff.2 (Nat.one_le_iff_ne_zero.2 hai))
  have hmi : m i + 1 = a i := by
    rw [hm, Finsupp.tsub_apply, Finsupp.single_eq_same]
    omega
  have hc := coeff_pderiv (i := i) f m
  have hc0 : (0 : MvPolynomial σ k).coeff m = 0 := by simp
  rw [h i, hc0, hma] at hc
  have hcast : ((m i : k) + 1) = (a i : k) := by rw [← hmi, Nat.cast_add, Nat.cast_one]
  rw [hcast] at hc
  have hne : f.coeff a ≠ 0 := mem_support_iff.1 ha
  exact (CharP.cast_eq_zero_iff k p _).1
    ((mul_eq_zero.1 hc.symm).resolve_left hne)

variable [PerfectRing k p]

/-- Over a perfect field of characteristic `p`, all the partial derivatives of `f` vanish if and
only if `f` is a `p`-th power. -/
theorem exists_eq_pow_iff_pderiv_eq_zero {f : MvPolynomial σ k} :
    (∃ g, f = g ^ p) ↔ ∀ i, pderiv i f = 0 := by
  classical
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨g, rfl⟩ i
    exact derivation_pow_char (pderiv i) g
  · intro h
    let d : (σ →₀ ℕ) → (σ →₀ ℕ) := Finsupp.mapRange (fun n => n / p) (Nat.zero_div p)
    have hd : ∀ a ∈ f.support, p • d a = a := by
      intro a ha
      ext i
      simp only [d, Finsupp.smul_apply, Finsupp.mapRange_apply, smul_eq_mul]
      exact Nat.mul_div_cancel' (dvd_of_pderiv_eq_zero h ha i)
    let h0 : MvPolynomial σ k := ∑ a ∈ f.support, monomial (d a) (f.coeff a)
    have hexp : expand p h0 = f := by
      simp only [h0, map_sum, expand_monomial]
      conv_rhs => rw [f.as_sum]
      exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun a ha => by rw [hd a ha]
    refine ⟨map (frobeniusEquiv k p).symm.toRingHom h0, ?_⟩
    have hcomp : (frobenius k p).comp (frobeniusEquiv k p).symm.toRingHom = RingHom.id k := by
      ext x
      simp
    rw [← map_frobenius_expand p, map_expand, map_map, hcomp, map_id, hexp]

/-- Over a perfect field of characteristic `p`, `J_Δ(f) = 0` if and only if `f` is a `p`-th
power in `k[x]` (Volume V, Lemma 4.4.4, part 2, polynomial model). -/
theorem logJacobian_eq_bot_iff [DecidableEq σ] {Δ : Finset σ} {f : MvPolynomial σ k} :
    logJacobian Δ f = ⊥ ↔ ∃ g, f = g ^ p := by
  rw [logJacobian_eq_bot_iff_pderiv, exists_eq_pow_iff_pderiv_eq_zero]

end Perfect

section Monomial

variable {σ k : Type*} [Field k] {p : ℕ} [CharP k p]

/-- **A first integral of monomial type gives a principal ideal**, in the polynomial model. Let
`t = x^a`, let `Δ` contain each `i` with `p ∤ a_i`, and let `p ∤ a_i` for some `i ∈ Δ`. Let
`f = ∑_{i < p} c_i^p t^i` with polynomials `c_i`, and `c = ∑_{i < p} i c_i^p t^(i-1)`. Then
`J_Δ(f) = (c t)` (Volume V, Proposition 4.4.15, part 1, with the unit `u = 1`). -/
theorem logJacobian_eq_span_of_monomial {a : σ →₀ ℕ} {Δ : Finset σ}
    (hout : ∀ i, i ∉ Δ → p ∣ a i) {i₀ : σ} (hi₀ : i₀ ∈ Δ) (hp : ¬ p ∣ a i₀)
    (c : Fin p → MvPolynomial σ k) :
    logJacobian Δ (∑ i : Fin p, c i ^ p * monomial a 1 ^ (i : ℕ)) =
      Ideal.span {(∑ i : Fin p, ((i : ℕ) : MvPolynomial σ k) * c i ^ p *
        monomial a 1 ^ ((i : ℕ) - 1)) * monomial a 1} := by
  set t : MvPolynomial σ k := monomial a 1 with ht
  set cf : MvPolynomial σ k :=
    ∑ i : Fin p, ((i : ℕ) : MvPolynomial σ k) * c i ^ p * t ^ ((i : ℕ) - 1) with hcf
  set f : MvPolynomial σ k := ∑ i : Fin p, c i ^ p * t ^ (i : ℕ) with hf
  have hd : ∀ j, pderiv j f = cf * pderiv j t := fun j => derivation_sum_pow_mul_pow _ c t
  have hx : ∀ j, X j * pderiv j t = ((a j : ℕ) : MvPolynomial σ k) * t := fun j => by
    rw [ht, X_mul_pderiv_monomial, nsmul_eq_mul]
  have hz : ∀ j, j ∉ Δ → pderiv j t = 0 := fun j hj => by
    rw [ht, pderiv_monomial, one_mul, (CharP.cast_eq_zero_iff k p _).2 (hout j hj),
      monomial_zero]
  refine le_antisymm (Ideal.span_le.2 ?_) ?_
  · rintro _ (⟨j, -, rfl⟩ | ⟨j, hj, rfl⟩)
    · show X j * pderiv j f ∈ Ideal.span {cf * t}
      rw [hd, mul_left_comm, hx, Ideal.mem_span_singleton]
      exact ⟨((a j : ℕ) : MvPolynomial σ k), by ring⟩
    · show pderiv j f ∈ Ideal.span {cf * t}
      rw [hd, hz j hj, mul_zero]
      exact zero_mem _
  · rw [Ideal.span_le, Set.singleton_subset_iff]
    have hmem : X i₀ * pderiv i₀ f ∈ logJacobian Δ f := Ideal.subset_span (Or.inl ⟨i₀, hi₀, rfl⟩)
    rw [hd, mul_left_comm, hx] at hmem
    have hu : ((a i₀ : ℕ) : k) ≠ 0 := fun h => hp ((CharP.cast_eq_zero_iff k p _).1 h)
    have hC : ((a i₀ : ℕ) : MvPolynomial σ k) = C ((a i₀ : ℕ) : k) := (map_natCast C _).symm
    have hinv : C ((a i₀ : ℕ) : k)⁻¹ * C ((a i₀ : ℕ) : k) = (1 : MvPolynomial σ k) := by
      rw [← C_mul, inv_mul_cancel₀ hu, C_1]
    have heq : cf * t = C ((a i₀ : ℕ) : k)⁻¹ * (cf * (((a i₀ : ℕ) : MvPolynomial σ k) * t)) := by
      rw [hC]
      linear_combination -(cf * t) * hinv
    show cf * t ∈ logJacobian Δ f
    rw [heq]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ hmem

end Monomial

/-! ### The derivations tangent to a center -/

section Center

variable {σ k : Type*} [CommRing k] [DecidableEq σ]

omit [DecidableEq σ] in
/-- A derivation maps the ideal `(x_l : l ∈ S)` into itself if and only if it maps each `x_l`,
`l ∈ S`, into it. -/
theorem mem_stableDerivations_span_X_iff {S : Set σ}
    {δ : Derivation k (MvPolynomial σ k) (MvPolynomial σ k)} :
    δ ∈ stableDerivations k (Ideal.span (X '' S)) ↔ ∀ l ∈ S, δ (X l) ∈ Ideal.span (X '' S) := by
  constructor
  · exact fun h l hl => h _ (Ideal.subset_span ⟨l, hl, rfl⟩)
  · intro h b hb
    induction hb using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem x hx =>
      obtain ⟨l, hl, rfl⟩ := hx
      exact h l hl
    | zero => rw [map_zero]; exact zero_mem _
    | add x y _ _ hx hy => rw [map_add]; exact add_mem hx hy
    | smul a x hx hih =>
      rw [smul_eq_mul, Derivation.leibniz, smul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul]
      exact add_mem (Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ hih) (Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ hx)

/-- The generators of the derivations tangent to the divisor `Δ` and to the center `S`:
`x_i ∂_i` for `i ∈ Δ`, `∂_l` for `l ∉ Δ`, `l ∉ S`, and `x_m ∂_l` for `l ∉ Δ`, `l ∈ S`,
`m ∈ S`. -/
abbrev centerDerivations (Δ S : Finset σ) :
    Set (Derivation k (MvPolynomial σ k) (MvPolynomial σ k)) :=
  (fun i => X (R := k) i • pderiv i) '' (Δ : Set σ) ∪
    (fun l => pderiv (R := k) l) '' {l | l ∉ Δ ∧ l ∉ S} ∪
    (fun a : σ × σ => X (R := k) a.1 • pderiv a.2) '' {a | a.2 ∉ Δ ∧ a.2 ∈ S ∧ a.1 ∈ S}

/-- **The log derivations tangent to the center** (Volume V, Lemma 4.4.18, part 1, polynomial
model). The derivations tangent to `x_i = 0` for `i ∈ Δ` that map `I_Z = (x_l : l ∈ S)` into
`I_Z` are generated by `x_i ∂_i` (`i ∈ Δ`), `∂_l` (`l ∉ Δ`, `l ∉ S`) and `x_m ∂_l` (`l ∉ Δ`,
`l ∈ S`, `m ∈ S`). -/
theorem tangentDerivations_inf_stable_eq_span [Fintype σ] (Δ S : Finset σ) :
    tangentDerivations k (X '' (Δ : Set σ)) ⊓ stableDerivations k (Ideal.span (X '' (S : Set σ)))
      = Submodule.span (MvPolynomial σ k) (centerDerivations (k := k) Δ S) := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun δ hδ => ?_) (Submodule.span_le.2 ?_)
  · obtain ⟨hT, hS⟩ := Submodule.mem_inf.1 hδ
    rw [derivation_eq_sum_pderiv δ]
    refine Submodule.sum_mem _ fun i _ => ?_
    by_cases hi : i ∈ Δ
    · obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.1 (mem_tangentDerivations_X_iff.1 hT i hi)
      rw [← hc, mul_smul]
      exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.subset_span (Or.inl (Or.inl ⟨i, hi, rfl⟩)))
    by_cases hiS : i ∈ S
    · have key : ∀ b ∈ Ideal.span (X (R := k) '' (S : Set σ)), b • pderiv (R := k) i ∈
          Submodule.span (MvPolynomial σ k) (centerDerivations (k := k) Δ S) := by
        intro b hb
        induction hb using Submodule.span_induction with
        | mem x hx =>
          obtain ⟨m, hm, rfl⟩ := hx
          exact Submodule.subset_span (Or.inr ⟨(m, i), ⟨hi, hiS, hm⟩, rfl⟩)
        | zero => rw [zero_smul]; exact zero_mem _
        | add x y _ _ hx hy => rw [add_smul]; exact add_mem hx hy
        | smul a x _ hih => rw [smul_eq_mul, mul_smul]; exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ hih
      exact key _ (mem_stableDerivations_span_X_iff.1 hS i hiS)
    · exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.subset_span (Or.inl (Or.inr ⟨i, ⟨hi, hiS⟩, rfl⟩)))
  · rintro _ ((⟨i, -, rfl⟩ | ⟨l, ⟨hlΔ, hlS⟩, rfl⟩) | ⟨⟨m, l⟩, ⟨hlΔ, -, hmS⟩, rfl⟩)
    · refine Submodule.mem_inf.2 ⟨X_smul_pderiv_mem_tangentDerivations _ i,
        mem_stableDerivations_span_X_iff.2 fun l hl => ?_⟩
      rw [smul_pderiv_X]
      split_ifs with h
      · subst h
        exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨l, hl, rfl⟩
      · exact zero_mem _
    · refine Submodule.mem_inf.2 ⟨pderiv_mem_tangentDerivations hlΔ,
        mem_stableDerivations_span_X_iff.2 fun m hm => ?_⟩
      have hml : m ≠ l := fun h => hlS (h ▸ hm)
      rw [pderiv_X_of_ne hml]
      exact zero_mem _
    · refine Submodule.mem_inf.2 ⟨mem_tangentDerivations_X_iff.2 fun i hi => ?_,
        mem_stableDerivations_span_X_iff.2 fun m' _ => ?_⟩
      · have hil : i ≠ l := fun h => hlΔ (h ▸ hi)
        show (X m • pderiv l) (X i) ∈ _
        simp only [smul_pderiv_X, hil, ↓reduceIte]
        exact zero_mem _
      · show (X m • pderiv l) (X m') ∈ _
        rw [smul_pderiv_X]
        split_ifs
        · exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨m, hmS, rfl⟩
        · exact zero_mem _

/-- The values at `g` of the log derivations tangent to the center give the ideal
`logJacobianCenter Δ S g` (Volume V, Lemma 4.4.18, part 1, polynomial model). -/
theorem derivationIdeal_center [Fintype σ] (Δ S : Finset σ) (g : MvPolynomial σ k) :
    derivationIdeal k (tangentDerivations k (X '' (Δ : Set σ)) ⊓
      stableDerivations k (Ideal.span (X '' (S : Set σ)))) g = logJacobianCenter Δ S g := by
  rw [derivationIdeal, tangentDerivations_inf_stable_eq_span, Submodule.map_span,
    centerDerivations, Set.image_union, Set.image_union, Set.image_image, Set.image_image,
    Set.image_image, logJacobianCenter]
  rfl

omit [DecidableEq σ] in
/-- If the center is a stratum of the divisor, `S ⊆ Δ`, then each log derivation maps `I_Z`
into `I_Z`. -/
theorem tangentDerivations_le_stable {Δ S : Finset σ} (h : S ⊆ Δ) :
    tangentDerivations k (X (R := k) '' (Δ : Set σ)) ≤
      stableDerivations k (Ideal.span (X '' (S : Set σ))) := by
  intro δ hδ
  refine mem_stableDerivations_span_X_iff.2 fun l hl => ?_
  exact Ideal.span_mono (Set.singleton_subset_iff.2 (Set.mem_image_of_mem X hl))
    (mem_tangentDerivations_X_iff.1 hδ l (h hl))

/-- For a center that is a stratum of the divisor, `S ⊆ Δ`, the ideal `J_{D,Z}(g)` is `J_D(g)`
(Volume V, Corollary 4.4.19, part 2, first claim, polynomial model). -/
theorem logJacobianCenter_of_subset [Fintype σ] {Δ S : Finset σ} (h : S ⊆ Δ)
    (g : MvPolynomial σ k) : logJacobianCenter Δ S g = logJacobian Δ g := by
  rw [← derivationIdeal_center, inf_eq_left.2 (tangentDerivations_le_stable h),
    derivationIdeal_tangentDerivations_X]

end Center

end Singularity
